@host = http://localhost:5187

# Story 11 - the Customers module: profile, contacts, notes, duplicate warning, search, scope. Run top to bottom against a
# Development API (`docker compose up -d`, then `dotnet run --project backend/src/Crm.Api --launch-profile http`).
# Dev seed (Crm.Modules.Customers.Contracts.DevSeed.CustomersDevSeed): Ahmed Al-Qahtani (individual, RYD-CARE, portal access),
# Najd Logistics (organisation, RYD-CARE, two contacts, one pinned note), Red Sea Trading (organisation, JED-CARE - invisible
# to agent A); Story 59 adds Al-Noor Clinics, Faisal Al-Dosari (both RYD-CARE) and Gulf Retail (RYD-BILL). On a fresh database the
# seed takes C-000001..C-000006, so request 6 is C-000007.
# Access tokens live 2 minutes in Development - re-run the logins when a request answers 401. Sign-in is limited to 30/min.
# rowVersion is base64: always send the value the LAST response returned (the requests below chain it with `# @name`).
# Every customer row is organisation-scoped (Story 06): an out-of-scope id is 403 Organisation.OutOfScope, an unknown id 404.

@ryCare = 06000000-0000-0000-0002-000000000001
@ryBill = 06000000-0000-0000-0002-000000000002
@jeCare = 06000000-0000-0000-0002-000000000003
@ahmed = 11000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@najd = 11000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002
@redSea = 11000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003
@unknown = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-00000000dead

### Login as agent A (Agent in RYD-CARE)
# @name loginAgentA
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "agent.a@crm.local", "password": "Crm_Dev_2026!" }

@agentAToken = {{loginAgentA.response.body.accessToken}}

### Login as agent B (Agent in JED-CARE)
# @name loginAgentB
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "agent.b@crm.local", "password": "Crm_Dev_2026!" }

@agentBToken = {{loginAgentB.response.body.accessToken}}

### Login as supervisor (Supervisor in RYD-CARE, Agent in RYD-BILL)
# @name loginSupervisor
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "supervisor@crm.local", "password": "Crm_Dev_2026!" }

@supervisorToken = {{loginSupervisor.response.body.accessToken}}

### 1. List as agent A - 200: Ahmed and Najd, NOT Red Sea. EF log WHERE has [c].[IsDeleted] = CAST(0 AS bit), [c].[TenantId] = @...,
### [c].[BranchId] = @..., [c].[DepartmentId] = @... (scope in SQL).
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 2. Arabic search (أحمد, percent-encoded) - 200: Ahmed Al-Qahtani
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers?search=%D8%A3%D8%AD%D9%85%D8%AF
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 3a. Search by English name - 200: Najd Logistics
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers?search=Najd
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 3b. Search by customer number - 200: four rows visible to agent A (C-000001, C-000002, C-000004, C-000005; C-000003 is Jeddah and C-000006 is Billing, so not visible)
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers?search=C-00000
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 3c. Search by email fragment - 200: Najd. EF log: EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM [customers].[CustomerContacts] ... [Email] LIKE ...)
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers?search=najd.example
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 3d. Search by phone, separators ignored (50 123 4567) - 200: Ahmed
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers?search=50%20123%204567
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 4a. Filtered, sorted, paged - 200: page 1 of 1 item, total = the unpaged count. EF log: ORDER BY [c].[DisplayNameEn], [c].[Number] + OFFSET/FETCH
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers?status=Active&sort=nameEn&descending=false&page=1&pageSize=1
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 4b. Page 2 - 200: a different customer
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers?status=Active&sort=nameEn&descending=false&page=2&pageSize=1
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 4c. Bad paging and sort - 400 urn:crm:problem:validation: errors.PageSize, errors.Sort (custom text)
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers?pageSize=0&sort=nope
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 5. Lookup for the ticket customer picker - 200: active customers only
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/lookup?search=na&take=5
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 6. Create an individual with two contacts - 200 created: true, number C-000007 on a fresh DB, contact 1 primary automatically,
### email stored lower-case, phone +966550001111 (separators stripped), contact 2 email: null (phone-only)
# @name layla
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{
  "displayNameEn": "Layla Hassan",
  "type": "Individual",
  "preferredLanguage": "en",
  "contacts": [
    { "name": "Layla Hassan", "email": "Layla.Hassan@Example.com" },
    { "name": "Layla mobile", "phone": "+966 55 000 1111" }
  ]
}

@lay = {{layla.response.body.customer.id}}

### 7. Create with a contact email that already exists in scope (ahmed@example.com), no confirmation - 200 created: false,
### customer: null, duplicateCandidates[0] = Ahmed with matchedEmails ["ahmed@example.com"]. Nothing is written.
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "displayNameEn": "Ahmed Again", "type": "Individual", "preferredLanguage": "en", "contacts": [{ "name": "Ahmed", "email": "ahmed@example.com" }] }

### 8. Same body, confirmDuplicate: true - 200 created: true
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "displayNameEn": "Ahmed Again", "type": "Individual", "preferredLanguage": "en", "confirmDuplicate": true, "contacts": [{ "name": "Ahmed", "email": "ahmed@example.com" }] }

### 9. Request 7's body as agent B - 200 created: true in JED-CARE: Ahmed is outside B's scope, so there is no warning
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentBToken}}

{ "displayNameEn": "Ahmed Again", "type": "Individual", "preferredLanguage": "en", "contacts": [{ "name": "Ahmed", "email": "ahmed@example.com" }] }

### 10. Organisation without a legal name - 422 urn:crm:problem:domain-rule, code Customers.LegalNameRequired (the validator allows it; the aggregate refuses)
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "displayNameEn": "No Legal Name Co", "type": "Organisation", "preferredLanguage": "en" }

### 11. Individual with a legal name - 422 Customers.LegalNameNotAllowed
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "displayNameEn": "Person", "type": "Individual", "legalName": "Person Ltd", "preferredLanguage": "en" }

### 12a. Malformed email - 422 Customers.EmailInvalid (rejected by the EmailAddress value object, not by a validator)
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "displayNameEn": "Bad Email", "type": "Individual", "preferredLanguage": "en", "contacts": [{ "name": "N", "email": "not-an-email" }] }

### 12b. Phone without a country code - 422 Customers.PhoneInvalid
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "displayNameEn": "Bad Phone", "type": "Individual", "preferredLanguage": "en", "contacts": [{ "name": "N", "phone": "0501234567" }] }

### 13. Two contacts whose emails differ only by case - 422 Customers.DuplicateContactEmail
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "displayNameEn": "Twin Emails", "type": "Individual", "preferredLanguage": "en", "contacts": [{ "name": "A", "email": "a@x.example" }, { "name": "B", "email": "A@X.example" }] }

### 14a. Contact with neither email nor phone - 422 Customers.ContactChannelRequired
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "displayNameEn": "No Channel", "type": "Individual", "preferredLanguage": "en", "contacts": [{ "name": "A" }] }

### 14b. Portal access with a phone only - 422 Customers.PortalAccessRequiresEmail
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "displayNameEn": "Portal Phone", "type": "Individual", "preferredLanguage": "en", "contacts": [{ "name": "A", "phone": "+966500000001", "hasPortalAccess": true }] }

### 15a. No names - 400 urn:crm:problem:validation, errors.DisplayNameEn (custom, localised text)
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "type": "Individual", "preferredLanguage": "en" }

### 15b. Unknown type - 400 errors.Type
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "displayNameEn": "Robot", "type": "Robot", "preferredLanguage": "en" }

### 15c. Unsupported language - 400 errors.PreferredLanguage (custom, localised text)
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "displayNameEn": "French", "type": "Individual", "preferredLanguage": "fr" }

### 16. Get by id - run TWICE: 200 both times, ONE `SELECT ... FROM [customers].[Customers]` in the EF log across both (cached, culture-neutral)
# @name cached
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{lay}}
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 17. Update the profile (new Arabic name) with the current rowVersion - 200, modifiedBy set, new rowVersion. EF log: INSERT INTO
### [customers].[outbox_messages] inside the transaction. Then re-run request 16: a fresh SELECT and the new name.
# @name updated
PUT {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{lay}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "displayNameAr": "ليلى حسن", "displayNameEn": "Layla Hassan", "type": "Individual", "preferredLanguage": "en", "rowVersion": "{{cached.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

### 17b. Stale rowVersion - 409 Persistence.ConcurrencyConflict
PUT {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{lay}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "displayNameEn": "Stale", "type": "Individual", "preferredLanguage": "en", "rowVersion": "AAAAAAAAB9E=" }

### 18a. Deactivate - 200 status Inactive
# @name deactivated
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{lay}}/deactivate
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "rowVersion": "{{updated.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

### 18b. Deactivate again - 422 Customers.AlreadyInactive
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{lay}}/deactivate
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "rowVersion": "{{deactivated.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

### 18c. Reactivate - 200 status Active
# @name reactivated
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{lay}}/reactivate
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "rowVersion": "{{deactivated.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

### 18d. Reactivate again - 422 Customers.AlreadyActive
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{lay}}/reactivate
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "rowVersion": "{{reactivated.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

### 19. Add a primary contact - 200: the new contact isPrimary true and the previous primary false, in ONE response. EF log: UPDATE
### [customers].[Customers] SET ... [Revision] ... WHERE [Id] = @... AND [RowVersion] = @... and INSERT INTO [customers].[CustomerContacts]
### in one transaction (a child-only change is concurrency-checked).
# @name withWork
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{lay}}/contacts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "name": "Layla work", "email": "layla@work.example", "isPrimary": true, "hasPortalAccess": false, "rowVersion": "{{reactivated.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

@workContact = {{withWork.response.body.contacts[0].id}}
@otherContact = {{withWork.response.body.contacts[1].id}}

### 20a. Add a contact with an email another contact already has - 422 Customers.DuplicateContactEmail
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{lay}}/contacts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "name": "Dup", "email": "layla.hassan@example.com", "isPrimary": false, "hasPortalAccess": false, "rowVersion": "{{withWork.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

### 20b. Add a contact with a phone another contact already has - 422 Customers.DuplicateContactPhone
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{lay}}/contacts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "name": "Dup", "phone": "+966550001111", "isPrimary": false, "hasPortalAccess": false, "rowVersion": "{{withWork.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

### 21a. Update a contact (rename, grant portal access) - 200
# @name renamedContact
PUT {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{lay}}/contacts/{{otherContact}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "name": "Layla H.", "email": "layla.hassan@example.com", "hasPortalAccess": true, "rowVersion": "{{withWork.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

### 21b. Change its email to another contact's - 422 Customers.DuplicateContactEmail
PUT {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{lay}}/contacts/{{otherContact}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "name": "Layla H.", "email": "layla@work.example", "hasPortalAccess": false, "rowVersion": "{{renamedContact.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

### 22. Make the other contact primary - 200: primary moved, exactly one isPrimary
# @name movedPrimary
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{lay}}/contacts/{{otherContact}}/primary
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "rowVersion": "{{renamedContact.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

### 23a. Remove the primary contact while others exist - 422 Customers.PrimaryContactRemoval
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{lay}}/contacts/{{otherContact}}/remove
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "rowVersion": "{{movedPrimary.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

### 23b. Remove a non-primary contact - 200
# @name removedContact
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{lay}}/contacts/{{workContact}}/remove
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "rowVersion": "{{movedPrimary.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

### 24. Unknown contact - 404 Customers.ContactNotFound
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{lay}}/contacts/{{unknown}}/primary
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "rowVersion": "{{removedContact.response.body.rowVersion}}" }

### 25a. Add a note - 200 (notes take no rowVersion and never 409 between agents)
# @name noteFirst
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{lay}}/notes
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "body": "first" }

@firstNote = {{noteFirst.response.body.notes[0].id}}

### 25b. Add a second, newer note - 200: notes newest first ("second" above "first")
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{lay}}/notes
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "body": "second" }

### 25c. Pin the first note - 200: notes[0] is "first" (pinned above the newer "second")
PUT {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{lay}}/notes/{{firstNote}}/pin
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "isPinned": true }

### 25d. Get - the pinned note is still first
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{lay}}
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 25e. Unpin - 200: "second" is first again
PUT {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{lay}}/notes/{{firstNote}}/pin
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "isPinned": false }

### 25f. Remove the note - 200 (the row is deleted)
DELETE {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{lay}}/notes/{{firstNote}}
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 25g. Remove an unknown note - 404 Customers.NoteNotFound
DELETE {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{lay}}/notes/{{unknown}}
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 26. Add a contact with a stale rowVersion - 409 Persistence.ConcurrencyConflict (a child change is concurrency-checked too)
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{lay}}/contacts
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

{ "name": "Stale", "email": "stale@x.example", "isPrimary": false, "hasPortalAccess": false, "rowVersion": "AAAAAAAAB9E=" }

### 27a. As agent B, GET Ahmed (RYD-CARE) - 403 Organisation.OutOfScope
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{ahmed}}
Authorization: Bearer {{agentBToken}}

### 27b. As agent B, PUT Ahmed - 403
PUT {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{ahmed}}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentBToken}}

{ "displayNameEn": "Hijacked", "type": "Individual", "preferredLanguage": "en", "rowVersion": "AAAAAAAAB9E=" }

### 27c. As agent B, add a note to Ahmed - 403
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{ahmed}}/notes
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentBToken}}

{ "body": "not mine" }

### 27d. As agent B, deactivate Ahmed - 403
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{ahmed}}/deactivate
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentBToken}}

{ "rowVersion": "AAAAAAAAB9E=" }

### 27e. As agent B, create into RYD-CARE - 403 Organisation.OutOfScope (write into a foreign department)
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{agentBToken}}

{ "displayNameEn": "B into A", "type": "Individual", "preferredLanguage": "en", "departmentId": "{{ryCare}}" }

### 28. Unknown id - 404 Customers.CustomerNotFound (never confused with the 403 above)
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers/{{unknown}}
Authorization: Bearer {{agentAToken}}

### 29a. Supervisor (two departments), no X-Crm-Scope, no departmentId - 400 Organisation.DepartmentRequired
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisorToken}}

{ "displayNameEn": "Ambiguous", "type": "Individual", "preferredLanguage": "en" }

### 29b. Supervisor with X-Crm-Scope: RYD-BILL - 200, the customer lands in RYD-BILL
POST {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{supervisorToken}}
X-Crm-Scope: {{ryBill}}

{ "displayNameEn": "Billing customer", "type": "Individual", "preferredLanguage": "en" }

### 30. No token - 401 urn:crm:problem:unauthorized
GET {{host}}/api/Agent/Customers
